the subcontracting goals pertain to more than one contract with one or more Federal agencies, or to one contract with more than one Federal agency, the prime contractor may only receive credit for first tier subcontractors that are small business concerns.\",\"references\":[\"paragraph (6)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:a6a45cbee9ac935853c33a34588feb320d05dbc9351a75f8ba4ff59467975d5f\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(A) In general.— For purposes of determining whether or not a prime contractor has attained the percentage goals specified in paragraph (6)—\",\"(ii) if the subcontracting goals pertain to more than one contract with one or more Federal agencies, or to one contract with more than one Federal agency, the prime contractor may only receive credit for first tier subcontractors that are small business concerns.\"],\"scope_text\":\"For purposes of determining whether or not a prime contractor has attained the percentage goals specified in paragraph (6), if the subcontracting goals pertain to more than one contract with one or more Federal agencies, or to one contract with more than one Federal agency\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":623,\"summary\":\"For purposes of determining whether or not a prime contractor has attained the percentage goals specified in paragraph (6), if the subcontracting goals pertain to more than one contract with one or more Federal agencies, or to one contract with more than one Federal agency, the prime contractor may only receive credit for first tier subcontractors that are small business concerns.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"term_refs\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
